==English==

===Etymology===
{{term|gastro-|lang=en}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|γαστήρ||belly|tr=gastēr|lang=grc}} + {{term|enterology|lang=en}}, from {{term|entero-|lang=en}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ἔντερον||intestine|tr=enteron|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}
{{wikipedia}}

# The study of the [[digestive]] system, from mouth to anus.  May also include the study of accessory organs: pancreas, liver, gallbladder and bile ducts.

